WEBVTT

0:00:08.650 --> 0:00:11.059
♫ Magic stack of old cards ♫

0:00:11.060 --> 0:00:13.060
♫ From the Fortune Teller, ♫

0:00:13.070 --> 0:00:15.440
♫ Eight clones summoned to this world, ♫

0:00:15.440 --> 0:00:16.810
♫ And every one of them: ♫

0:00:16.810 --> 0:00:17.939
♫ A different look, ♫

0:00:17.940 --> 0:00:18.980
♫ A different hook, ♫

0:00:18.980 --> 0:00:20.100
♫ And different outlook ♫

0:00:20.100 --> 0:00:21.160
♫ On what’s good ♫

0:00:21.160 --> 0:00:23.290
♫ And who’s the king, and who’s the jack, ♫

0:00:23.390 --> 0:00:25.520
♫ Wish you good luck on keeping track! ♫

0:00:25.750 --> 0:00:27.730
♫ What could possibly go wrong? ♫

0:00:27.740 --> 0:00:29.850
♫ What could possibly go wrong? ♫

0:00:29.860 --> 0:00:31.940
♫ What could possibly go wrong? ♫

0:00:31.950 --> 0:00:34.730
♫  EVERYTHING WENT WRONG! ♫

0:00:37.000 --> 0:00:39.604
I WILL LITERALLY KILL YOU, CHARLIE!

0:00:39.604 --> 0:00:40.800
THAT’S A FELONY, RICCARDO!

0:00:40.810 --> 0:00:41.729
What’s all that noise

0:00:41.729 --> 0:00:42.450
Where is it?..

0:00:42.450 --> 0:00:44.560
There’s no foooood!

0:00:47.690 --> 0:00:50.230
Peppers, cabbage, eggplant.

0:00:50.230 --> 0:00:52.690
There’s absolutely nothing to eat!

0:00:53.020 --> 0:00:55.270
Do you not like your greens, Waru?

0:00:55.520 --> 0:00:57.730
I do, but the other kind.

0:00:58.020 --> 0:00:59.980
Why don’t we order something in?

0:00:59.980 --> 0:01:01.520
That’s a great idea!

0:01:01.770 --> 0:01:05.689
Fёdor didn’t like us spending money on takeaway.

0:01:05.800 --> 0:01:07.440
Are you suggesting we finish the pasta?

0:01:08.560 --> 0:01:09.729
Fine, you won.

0:01:10.100 --> 0:01:12.729
And this needs to be destroyed.

0:01:12.980 --> 0:01:13.700
Eugh…

0:01:13.950 --> 0:01:14.939
What do we order?

0:01:15.150 --> 0:01:16.520
How about pizza?

0:01:16.650 --> 0:01:18.230
I want suuuushi!

0:01:18.600 --> 0:01:20.689
But sushi don’t want you!

0:01:22.690 --> 0:01:24.060
You can do better than that.

0:01:24.060 --> 0:01:25.850
It’s all because I’m hungry!

0:01:26.190 --> 0:01:30.650
This monster needs protein! Carbs!

0:01:30.650 --> 0:01:33.729
Uh…! What else is there? Help me out, Kuromaku!

0:01:34.190 --> 0:01:36.312
Polyunsaturated fats, amino acids…

0:01:36.590 --> 0:01:37.689
Shut it, Kuromaku!

0:01:40.270 --> 0:01:41.229
What did you say?

0:01:41.230 --> 0:01:42.810
You shut it, you!

0:01:43.100 --> 0:01:44.650
This isn’t my forte

0:01:44.650 --> 0:01:45.104
yeah!

0:01:45.660 --> 0:01:46.729
you green little…

0:01:46.730 --> 0:01:48.230
Come on, put ‘em up!

0:01:52.800 --> 0:01:53.270
Ha!

0:01:53.270 --> 0:01:56.020
Two down! More for us…

0:01:56.900 --> 0:01:58.940
Come on! High five!

0:01:58.950 --> 0:02:01.729
You stuck a push pin to your hand.

0:02:01.730 --> 0:02:05.060
You were way more fun without the glasses!...

0:02:09.020 --> 0:02:09.940
Dante!

0:02:10.440 --> 0:02:11.350
Can I come with?

0:02:15.310 --> 0:02:17.520
So… Are you taking a walk?

0:02:17.770 --> 0:02:19.850
Yes, it’s a delightful evening.

0:02:19.850 --> 0:02:21.190
hat’s true…uhhh?

0:02:21.400 --> 0:02:26.349
What happened to: “Evening strolls pave the way - for your gland's health every day”?

0:02:27.350 --> 0:02:29.310
Do you mind if we stop over somewhere?

0:02:31.520 --> 0:02:32.810
Who wants what?

0:02:33.230 --> 0:02:35.150
I want more meat!

0:02:35.150 --> 0:02:36.730
I want more cheese!

0:02:36.900 --> 0:02:38.480
I want MORE!

0:02:38.480 --> 0:02:39.480
I want.

0:02:39.480 --> 0:02:40.190
I. 

0:02:42.730 --> 0:02:45.150
Okay, they have something new! Pizza…

0:02:45.150 --> 0:02:47.230
with pears?

0:02:47.480 --> 0:02:50.099
Ew! What kind of pervert came up with that?!

0:02:50.100 --> 0:02:51.400
That’s sickening…

0:02:51.700 --> 0:02:53.020
Sraephtiw???

0:02:53.940 --> 0:02:55.730
How about Hawaiian?

0:02:55.980 --> 0:02:57.940
Oh, pineapples! Pineapples!

0:02:57.940 --> 0:02:59.310
It has chicken in it.

0:03:00.100 --> 0:03:02.200
THE WORLD HAS GONE MAD!

0:03:02.350 --> 0:03:03.310
I worked it out!

0:03:03.650 --> 0:03:07.189
“Sraephtiw” is “with pears” backwards.

0:03:07.689 --> 0:03:08.230
Agh.

0:03:10.060 --> 0:03:11.230
Pepperoni’s on its way!

0:03:16.310 --> 0:03:20.900
Normally I feel anxious at night, but today I feel calm…

0:03:25.100 --> 0:03:26.100
The first snow!

0:03:27.100 --> 0:03:29.400
Looks like winter came early.

0:03:30.812 --> 0:03:32.646
I'm only interested in the bent Criminal Artists, let's go!

0:03:32.810 --> 0:03:33.980
Finally!

0:03:33.980 --> 0:03:34.900
I’ll get it!

0:03:35.940 --> 0:03:37.480
We don’t have enough stools

0:03:37.770 --> 0:03:38.440
Where are they?

0:03:38.440 --> 0:03:39.437
On the balcony.

0:03:39.550 --> 0:03:40.730
I’ll go get them.

0:03:43.100 --> 0:03:43.940
Wait…

0:03:44.770 --> 0:03:48.440
We usually eat in front of the TV… On the sofa…

0:03:48.730 --> 0:03:50.440
Waru, no Waru!…

0:03:51.650 --> 0:03:53.650
I’m taking your slice!

0:03:53.650 --> 0:03:56.269
You can have it, just let me back in!

0:03:56.270 --> 0:03:59.020
You know too much!

0:04:00.060 --> 0:04:01.980
Gabriel! Open the door!

0:04:05.689 --> 0:04:06.900
Spade!

0:04:07.700 --> 0:04:09.230
Spade, open the door!

0:04:09.400 --> 0:04:12.150
He wrote us into his will.

0:04:12.600 --> 0:04:14.150
Pah! Nice.

0:04:16.830 --> 0:04:19.729
Oh, Fedya! You’re back early!

0:04:21.560 --> 0:04:26.900
Oh, right…  you’re a courier… What a coincidence, isn’t it?

0:04:26.900 --> 0:04:28.690
Seriously?

0:04:28.690 --> 0:04:32.190
I work evenings just so you could spend my money on takeaway?

0:04:33.020 --> 0:04:35.020
But we’re bad at cooking!

0:04:35.020 --> 0:04:36.521
Well, you should learn!

0:04:37.350 --> 0:04:39.900
Whatever, we’ll talk when I get back!

0:04:40.270 --> 0:04:41.099
Wait!

0:04:41.520 --> 0:04:43.099
Here’s your tip!

0:04:43.480 --> 0:04:46.810
But I don’t have… Romeo?

0:04:47.770 --> 0:04:50.270
Fedya, can I borrow some?

0:04:50.560 --> 0:04:51.940
Alright…

0:04:51.940 --> 0:04:52.810
Thank you!

0:04:57.310 --> 0:04:59.690
Here are my tips! Bye!

0:05:01.020 --> 0:05:03.520
Okay guys, pizza’s here! OUCH!-

0:05:09.100 --> 0:05:11.810
Have you ever noticed that the stars and snowflakes are similar?

0:05:12.600 --> 0:05:14.350
Even though they’re completely different.

0:05:14.900 --> 0:05:17.650
Snowflakes are so small and fragile.

0:05:18.060 --> 0:05:20.810
And the stars are so big and bright.

0:05:21.310 --> 0:05:26.900
But in our eyes they acquire common features and merge into one.

0:05:27.350 --> 0:05:31.520
It’s as if the stars fall from the sky so that everyone in the world gets a wish…

0:05:32.690 --> 0:05:33.520
Hmm…

0:05:33.770 --> 0:05:35.300
should we make a wish?

0:05:36.000 --> 0:05:37.300
Can’t see why not…

0:05:40.060 --> 0:05:42.310
Hey! Why are you two loitering?!

0:05:42.310 --> 0:05:44.310
This is a kids’ playground.

0:05:45.000 --> 0:05:49.190
All they do is break and break… they already broke them once…

0:05:54.520 --> 0:05:55.000
Huh?

0:05:55.000 --> 0:05:56.230
You’ve had enough!

0:05:56.230 --> 0:05:57.440
Hey! What?

0:05:57.440 --> 0:05:59.440
You’ve already had two slices!

0:05:59.440 --> 0:06:01.440
And I had the smallest one!

0:06:03.440 --> 0:06:04.850
That’s too easy!

0:06:05.150 --> 0:06:07.650
Either way, I’m still hungry!

0:06:08.020 --> 0:06:09.310
Why don’t you finish it then?

0:06:10.190 --> 0:06:11.560
I don’t like the crust…

0:06:12.000 --> 0:06:13.020
I call dibs!

0:06:13.020 --> 0:06:13.770
Ouch!

0:06:13.770 --> 0:06:14.599
Friends!

0:06:14.800 --> 0:06:18.349
It’s not right to fight over a slice of pizza…

0:06:18.810 --> 0:06:23.190
Let’s do the right thing and save it for the other guys when they come back!

0:06:23.500 --> 0:06:24.980
Hey, what the?!

0:06:25.230 --> 0:06:27.310
I SAID LET’S DO THE RIGHT THING!

0:06:30.100 --> 0:06:32.940
Looks like they’ll only let me in after I get frostbite…

0:06:34.440 --> 0:06:36.810
I have to move to stay alive.

0:06:41.000 --> 0:06:43.150
I DON’T need to move to stay alive…

0:06:49.400 --> 0:06:50.770
AHHHH!

0:06:51.350 --> 0:06:53.187
Kuromaku?! Where did you come from?!

0:06:53.600 --> 0:06:55.521
Obviously from up there.

0:06:57.700 --> 0:07:00.480
The higher you climb, the harder you fall.

0:07:00.480 --> 0:07:01.480
This again…

0:07:07.800 --> 0:07:10.150
Maybe… we could walk some more?

0:07:10.150 --> 0:07:13.810
Evening strolls pave the way - for your gland's health every day.

0:07:13.810 --> 0:07:15.350
Wait… that’s…

0:07:15.350 --> 0:07:17.850
In this case, I have to agree.

0:07:21.500 --> 0:07:25.310
Dante was talking to me today without using a single quote! Imagine that!

0:07:25.310 --> 0:07:28.350
Brolly, I’m only just starting to develop an imagination.

0:07:32.020 --> 0:07:34.849
Why did my courier rating drop after I delivered to you?! 

0:07:35.100 --> 0:07:37.560
I gave you two stars.

0:07:37.850 --> 0:07:38.650
Seriously?!

0:07:38.900 --> 0:07:40.350
Spade… Why?

0:07:40.560 --> 0:07:44.480
The pizza was cold, he ate one of the slices, and…

0:07:44.480 --> 0:07:45.480
he’s Fёdor.

0:07:45.810 --> 0:07:46.812
Yeah. Fair enough.

0:07:46.980 --> 0:07:47.400
Yeah.

0:07:48.250 --> 0:07:49.480
What? I’m honest.

0:07:53.730 --> 0:07:54.690
Gabriel?!

0:07:54.690 --> 0:07:55.350
Me?

0:07:55.900 --> 0:07:58.400
Are you out for a walk? I’ll get my jacket!

0:08:00.730 --> 0:08:01.480
Oh!

0:08:01.700 --> 0:08:02.770
I forgot my mittens! 

0:08:05.800 --> 0:08:06.479
Shall we?

0:08:07.520 --> 0:08:09.349
What’s going on with this tree?!

0:08:09.690 --> 0:08:12.100
It’s the stars…